==English==
[[Image:Kelis_perfect_smile.jpg|thumb|A '''smile''']]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)mey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|smilen|t=to smile}}, from {{der|en|gml|*smîlen|t=to smile}}, from {{der|en|gmh|smielen}}, from {{der|en|goh|smielēn}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*smilēn|*smīlēn}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*smilāną|*smīlāną|t=to smile}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*smey-|t=to laugh, be glad, wonder}}.

Cognate with {{cog|da|smile}}, {{cog|sv|smila}}, {{cog|fo|smíla|t=to smile}}; also {{cog|stq|smielje|t=to smile}}, {{cog|nds|smielen|t=to smile}}, {{cog|nl|smuilen|t=to smile}}, {{cog|gmh|smielen|t=to smile}}. Related also to {{cog|goh|smierōn|t=to smile}}, {{cog|ang|smerian|t=to laugh at}}, {{cog|ang|smercian}}, {{m|ang|smearcian}} {{gloss|"to smile"; > {{cog|en|smirk}}}}, {{cog|la|mīror|t=to wonder at}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsmaɪl/|/ˈsmaɪ.əl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-smile.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪl|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q487}}A facial [[expression]] comprised by [[flex]]ing the [[muscle]]s of both ends of one's [[mouth]], often showing the front [[tooth|teeth]], without [[vocalisation]], and in humans is a common involuntary or voluntary expression of [[happiness]], [[pleasure]], [[amusement]], [[goodwill]], or [[anxiety]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:smile}}
#: {{ux|en|She's got a perfect '''smile'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He has a sinister '''smile'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|She had a '''smile''' on her face.}}
#: {{ux|en|He always puts a '''smile''' on my face.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=Then came a maid with hand-bag and shawls, and after her a tall young lady.{{...}}She looked around expectantly, and recognizing Mrs. Cooke's maid{{...}}Miss Thorn greeted her with a '''smile''' which greatly prepossessed us in her favor.}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=Captain Edward Carlisle, soldier as he was, martinet as he was, felt a curious sensation of helplessness seize upon him as he met her steady gaze, her alluring '''smile'''; he could not tell what this prisoner might do.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[favour|Favour]]; propitious regard.
#: {{ux|en|the '''smile''' of the gods}}
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} A [[drink]] bought by one person for another.  <!--Chambers 1908-->
#: {{syn|en|treat}}

